# Complete local governing-definition bindings

The existing V2 and V3 reviewed-admission validators now require each RHS predicate matching a local definition to select exactly one matching declared parent. Matching includes the predicate name, ordered argument sorts and ordered argument roles. Missing or ambiguous selections refuse before reviewed semantic use. The existing declared dependency graph continues to own cycle detection and graph edges.

Fresh fictional signed assessments reproduced missing-parent acceptance in both domains. The final nine-case baseline had four passes and five failures. All nine passed with the shared validator. The complete V3 owning file passed 46 cases, including all 37 original cases. A separate earlier run passed 15 retained V2 cases with the same two implementation files. Earlier three-case and seven-case reproductions and every raw XML remain retained.

The positive controls preserve an explicitly selected later alternative, signed acyclic graph custody, and distinct predicates that share spelling but differ in roles or sorts. These checks establish software contract behavior with fictional sources and independent fixture signers. Canonical adoption, ordinary installed qualification, current physical Lean realization and substantive statutory review remain pending.
